  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following compound is added to the sodium extract before addition of silver nitrate for testing of halogens?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Nitric acid",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Sodium hydroxide",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Ammonia",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Hydrochloric acid",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For testing of halogens, Nitric acid is added to the sodium extract because if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>CN</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> are present then they will be oxidised and removed before the test of halides.</p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCN</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>NaNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>HCN</mi><mo>&#8593;</mo></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>NaNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#8593;</mo></math><br />Nilnic acid decomposed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCN</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>, else they precipitate in test &amp; misquite the resolve"
  }
}